  "lettering": [
    {
      "channel": "NARRATION",
      "id": "p32-narration",
      "placement": "caption-safe-region",
      "text": "Back at the hermitage, the fire has burned low. The listeners sit with the completed ending before asking what came later."
    },
    {
      "channel": "DIALOGUE",
      "id": "p32-extra-01",
      "placement": "closing-summary-balloon",
      "speaker_id": "dm-medhas",
      "text": "That is how Mahishasura's rule was broken. The gods asked for aid in calamity. Devi granted their request, and she vanished from their sight."
    },
    {
      "channel": "DIALOGUE",
      "id": "p32-extra-02",
      "placement": "listener-balloon",
      "speaker_id": "dm-samadhi",
      "text": "So the story ends not with another blow, but with remembrance."
    },
    {
      "channel": "INSET_EXPLANATION",
      "id": "p32-extra-03",
      "placement": "labeled-modern-editorial-reflection-inset",
      "text": "A danger may change shape. Courage works best with attention: when a problem changes, look again before acting. This is a modern editorial reflection, not scripture or doctrine."
    },
    {
      "channel": "DIALOGUE",
      "id": "p32-extra-04",
      "placement": "resolution-balloon",
      "speaker_id": "dm-medhas",
      "text": "Let the story rest there."
    },
    {
      "channel": "DIALOGUE",
      "id": "p32-extra-05",
      "placement": "next-story-question-balloon",
      "speaker_id": "dm-suratha",
      "text": "Did the gods ever need her again?"
    },
    {
      "channel": "DIALOGUE",
      "id": "p32-extra-06",
      "placement": "next-volume-transition-balloon",
      "speaker_id": "dm-medhas",
      "text": "They did. Later, when another danger arose, the Goddess would emerge from Gauri. But that is another story, and it begins on another evening."
    }
  ],
